WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:12.570
Hi! I walk to school every day. My sister does too: she walks to school. Why the extra s? Today we'll learn the simple present tense.

2
00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:17.154
For things we do every day or often, use the simple present.

3
00:00:17.304 --> 00:00:21.138
Words like every day, always and often are clues.

4
00:00:21.288 --> 00:00:25.602
We also use it for facts: the sun rises in the east.

5
00:00:25.752 --> 00:00:30.666
After I, you, we and they, the verb stays the same.

6
00:00:30.816 --> 00:00:35.658
For one person or thing, he, she or it, add s: she walks.

7
00:00:35.808 --> 00:00:41.394
Verbs ending in sh, ch or o add es: watches, goes.

8
00:00:41.544 --> 00:00:45.978
Consonant plus y becomes ies, and have becomes has.

9
00:00:46.128 --> 00:00:51.930
In the negative, she does not like milk: no s on the verb.

10
00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:57.354
Watch out! My brother is one person, so the verb needs an s!

11
00:00:57.504 --> 00:01:01.410
One person, and something he does every day: plays.

12
00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:06.210
So it's My brother plays football every day.

13
00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:15.978
Your turn! Mei, ___, to school by bus. Go or goes? Pause and think.

14
00:01:16.128 --> 00:01:21.642
Mei is one person, so goes. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:21.792 --> 00:01:31.554
Another one! We, ___, our teeth every night. Which one? Pause and think.

16
00:01:31.704 --> 00:01:37.890
After we, the verb stays the same: brush. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:47.442
Here's another! The cat, ___, milk. Which one? Pause and think.

18
00:01:47.592 --> 00:01:53.442
One cat, so add s: likes. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:53.592 --> 00:02:03.114
Try one more! Dad, ___, a big car. Have or has? Pause and think.

20
00:02:03.264 --> 00:02:08.322
One person takes has. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:08.472 --> 00:02:17.778
Try one more! The baby, ___, at night. Which one? Pause and think.

22
00:02:17.928 --> 00:02:24.330
Change y to i and add es: cries. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:34.338
Try one more! Ravi does not, ___, fish. Eat or eats? Pause and think.

24
00:02:34.488 --> 00:02:40.938
After does not, use the base verb: eat. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:41.088 --> 00:02:50.274
Last one! The sun, ___, in the east. Which one? Pause and think.

26
00:02:50.424 --> 00:02:56.202
It's a fact about one sun: rises. Did you get it right?

27
00:02:56.352 --> 00:03:04.170
Remember: use the simple present for habits and facts; after he, she and it, add s or es.

28
00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:07.986
Say what you do every morning!

